        <headline>AOG SUPPORT - TSRV SYSTEMS - RH BLEED DUCT PRESSURE LOW IN CLIMB</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: ACMS REVIEW SHOWS RH BLEED PX DROPPING TO 0 PSI IN CLIMB AND RECOVERING. THIS WORK ORDER HAS BEEN RAISED TO ASSIST IN TROUBLESHOOTING.

HEALTH CHECK REQUIRED.

ACTION:  
1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08 ) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.
    
* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM  
    
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.
    
3. LEAK CHECK ALL RH HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:    
A) SENSE LINES BETWEEN BAR AND PCCV         
B) SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR

4. INSPECT THE #2 PCCV KISS SEAL IAW AMM 36-12-02. REPLACE IF NECESSARY

5. CLOSELY INSPECT RH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE.

6. CHECK BLEED AIR REGULATOR FOR D/S PORT LEAKAGE OR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.
 
7. IF NFF, REPLACE THE #2 BAR IAW AMM  36-11-03/401 AND #2 450F SENSOR IAW AMM 36-11-05/401.

8. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE.

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.  

**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
